// ============================================================================
// Projections · CONFIG (YAML)  (pure column views — no joins, no closures)
//
// Named views over YAML config (application.yml, etc.), for both the client
// (java_*) and any external library (lib_*). YAML carries Spring config and, for
// multi-service systems, the service URLs / topics / endpoints that link one
// service's producer to another's consumer. Interpretation (class-name -> type,
// placeholder grouping, cross-service matching) is a resolution-layer step.
//
// Conventions: views only; one raw base relation per rule body; provenance tag first.
//
// java_yaml_property cols (16):
//   0 key  1 value  2 valueType  3 depth  4 isListItem  5 listIndex  6 anchorName
//   7 isAlias  8 documentIndex  9 filePath  10 baseMservPath  11 startLine
//   12 endLine  13 parentPropertyHash  14 serviceVersionLinkHash  15 yamlPropertyUniqueHash
//
// java_yaml_value_segment cols (12):
//   0 segmentValue  1 segmentType  2 defaultValue  3 position  4 depth
//   5 parentSegmentLinkHash  6 yamlPropertyLinkHash  7 startLine  8 endLine
//   9 startColumn  10 endColumn  11 yamlValueSegmentUniqueHash
// ============================================================================

// ── yaml_prop(Prov, Key, Value, ValueType, IsListItem, ParentPropertyHash, FilePath, PropHash) ──
// A YAML property (key/value), its scalar type, whether it is a list item, and its
// parent property (YAML is hierarchical).
//
// ValueType (col 2, YamlValueType enum):
//   STRING, INTEGER, FLOAT, BOOLEAN, NULL, EMPTY, MAP, SEQUENCE
yaml_prop("client", key, value, valueType, isListItem, parent, filePath, h) :- java_yaml_property(key, value, valueType, _, isListItem, _, _, _, _, filePath, _, _, _, parent, _, h).

// ── yaml_segment(Prov, PropertyHash, SegmentValue, SegmentType, DefaultValue, ParentSegmentHash, SegHash) ──
// One segment of a YAML value — a LITERAL (may name a class) or a reference.
// SegmentType (col 1, YamlValueSegmentType enum):
//   LITERAL, ENV_VARIABLE, ENV_WITH_DEFAULT, PROPERTY_REFERENCE,
//   PROPERTY_REF_WITH_DEFAULT, EMPTY
yaml_segment("client", propHash, value, segType, default, parentSeg, h) :- java_yaml_value_segment(value, segType, default, _, _, parentSeg, propHash, _, _, _, _, h).
